  "notes": [
    "Release geometry (underground): centroid separation of B1 and B2 is 163.3 m against 160 m (arXiv:1905.10258) and 165 m (arXiv:2009.05515); the 2006 TDR map caption says 140 m, which the OSM unit footprints do not support (16 % off) and is not used as a check. The footprints are whole nuclear-island buildings (~228 m span), not reactor-building domes, so the centroid is a proxy for the core axis good to a few tens of metres."
